message: "If you use this software or methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "Reality Infrastructure: provenance-aware, contradiction-preserving belief computation for contested records"
authors:
  - family-names: "Pierce"
    given-names: "Irvin"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-31
repository-code: "https://github.com/reality-infrastructure/reality-infrastructure"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - provenance
  - transparency-log
  - RFC-9162
  - dempster-shafer
  - contested-records
  - rights-state
  - evidence-fusion
  - replayable-audit
abstract: "A reference implementation for computing justified beliefs over contested multi-source evidence. Evidence is typed by epistemic character (self-asserted, third-party attested, cryptographically signed, statutory registry), fused under the Denoeux cautious rule so that contradiction is preserved as a first-class state rather than resolved away, committed to an RFC 9162-style Merkle transparency log, and reconstructable via byte-identical replay. Domains of application include any record system where claims conflict: rights and licensing state, chain-of-title, consent and opt-out registries, compliance disclosure derivation."
